    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, with minimal structural impact \u2014 two files touched, one changed line each, no growth of any method or class:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string field to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java((owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThe \"email present\" check mirrors the existing `MembershipLevel.of` convention (non-null and non-blank), and the field is populated automatically wherever an owner is mapped to a DTO (GET, list, create, update). No new classes, no changes to the response functions.\n\nTests: the two new acceptance tests pass and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (2/2, 0 failures).",
